"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: `Godot v4.8.dev4.mono`, `Godot v4.7.2.stable.mono`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-9700 CPU @ 3.00GHz (8 threads) - 15.93 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nFirst, you need a folder which contains a nested folder which contains a `.gdignore` file and a lot of files (which get ignored).\n\nThen, if you select the non-nested folder in the file-system view, the editor will freeze temporarily, and after the freeze is finished, it will open the folder.\n\nSince the nested folder has a `.gdignore`, the files should not be freezing the file-system view.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a folder inside `res://`\n2. Create a nested folder inside the folder\n3. Put a `.gdignore` inside the nested folder\n4. Put lots of files inside the nested folder\n5. Select the original (parent) folder inside the file-system view\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIn this MRP example, I am using [`@icons` by Voxybuns](https://github.com/Voxybuns/at-icons).\n\n[svg-freeze.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32494960/svg-freeze.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starr